{
  "_comment": [
    "The canonical instrument reference seed (M6b-1, ED-017).",
    "",
    "DATA, NOT CODE. Adding an instrument is an edit to this file — doc 15 sequencing",
    "principle 4: 'widening the universe is a data-ops task, not an architecture change.'",
    "",
    "Every value here is OUR claim about an instrument's identity, authored from",
    "authoritative public reference. tools/verify_universe.py checks those claims against",
    "the vendor; it never generates them. A verification whose expected values came from",
    "the thing being verified would always pass and would verify nothing.",
    "",
    "`isin` is null where we hold no authoritative source for it. The vendor reports one",
    "for most equities, but adopting the vendor's value would make the check circular —",
    "and yfinance already returns a name/ISIN pair for LT.NS that may not agree",
    "(doc 05 finding 9). Null means 'not yet claimed', never 'has none'. The verification",
    "report lists the vendor's value as a candidate awaiting confirmation, which mirrors",
    "doc 04's authoritative/candidate tiering.",
    "",
    "Deliberate omissions: Tata Motors is absent because its 2025 demerger leaves the",
    "identity behind TATAMOTORS.NS unverifiable from here — seeding an entity mid",
    "corporate action is the exact failure this milestone exists to prevent.",
    "",
    "`reference_version` lives beside the data it versions, so changing the universe is",
    "one edit rather than two. Bumping it is not cosmetic: it is pinned into every",
    "AnalyticResult, and observations ingested under an older version raise the",
    "reference-drift flag at L6 until re-ingested."
  ],
